    action: "In long events drink when thirsty rather than on a fixed schedule, and treat any weight gain during an event as a warning sign; for hot events, learn the signs of exertional heat stroke (central-nervous-system change plus high core temperature), confirm the event has cold-water immersion on site, and cool before transport.",
