    description:
      "The IOC consensus statements of 2014, 2018 and 2023 define Relative Energy Deficiency in Sport as the syndrome of impaired health and performance caused by low energy availability — intake insufficient for exercise energy expenditure — affecting female and male athletes, with more than 170 original studies added between 2018 and 2023. Controlled work showed luteinizing-hormone pulsatility is disrupted below a threshold of energy availability, and cohort data show bone-stress injuries rise with the number of triad risk factors. The ACSM triad position stand and the Female Athlete Triad Coalition statements set out treatment centred on restoring energy availability. The boundary: this is a medical diagnosis; the shelf's job is to get you screened, not to self-treat.",
    action: "If you have two or more of: unexplained performance decline, menstrual disturbance or low libido, a bone-stress injury, frequent illness, or deliberate low intake with high training, book a sports-medicine physician and a sports dietitian this month, ask for a RED-S/triad risk assessment, and follow an energy-availability plan before adding any training.",
