    description:
      "A 2020 meta-analysis of music in exercise and sport found reliable benefits for affective valence, physical performance and perceived exertion, with small effects on oxygen consumption; the two-part review and the BASES expert statement describe how tempo, synchrony and personal meaning drive the effect. Crossover studies show preferred warm-up music raises motivation and bench-press and anaerobic performance relative to non-preferred music, and preferred volume improves rowing time-trial output. The boundary: many competitions forbid headphones and self-paced racing depends on internal cues, so some sessions should be done without music.",
